{# THE TAB STRIP — the sibling screens of wherever the viewer is.

   The shell owns the strip and not one tab in it. That sibling screens are an
   underlined row, that the row sits between the page head and the page body,
   that exactly one tab is lit, and that one tab is no strip at all: those are
   layout decisions with no second opinion worth having. WHICH screens a place
   has is the host's model of that place, and a shell carrying the list would
   need a release every time the host grew a screen.

   A TAB THE VIEWER MAY NOT HAVE IS ABSENT. Not greyed, not inert — absent. A
   greyed tab tells a ranger that a screen exists and they are not trusted with
   it, which is a worse product than not mentioning it; and the value object has
   no url-less form, so there is nothing here to grey out even by accident. The
   withholding happens in the source, before the shell ever sees the list. #}
{%- if tabs|length > 0 -%}
    <div class="atabs">
        {%- for tab in tabs -%}
            <a href="{{ tab.url }}"{{ tab.current ? ' class="on"' : '' }}>{{ tab.label }}</a>
        {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
{%- endif -%}
